A||||27||pHoOl||performance chips||||1||
Z||000000||pHoOl||06-22-2000||10:39 PM||||Does anyone have any recommendations on performance chips?  I have an 88GT with an auto.  Also, how much do they help?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-22-2000||11:15 PM||||Not much unless you are into drag racing and want to use more gas.||||reg||13
Z||000002||terryk||06-23-2000||01:53 AM||||By and large, GM does an excellent job of tuning the chips. GM tests something like 15 cars and uses the average calibration for produciton. It's possible to fine tune the chip to a particular car, but it won't make much difference.<P>Unless you do something significant to your engine to increase the air being sucked in, the chips don't do much. Some make you *think* something is better, but generally, it's not worth getting.<P>Now on turbo engines it's a different story, but for the Fiero, there's not much to gain by just installing a chip. <P>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000003||HYPTNOTiSE||06-23-2000||01:05 PM||||The only reason you should look into getting a performance chip is for some luxury options to make the car a little more smooth.  <BR>1st- To elimanate the ANNOYING throttle bump at 1600rpm when the injectors depressurize.<P>2nd- To eliminate the REv limiter, on 88's i dont think it matters cos i've heard there is none or that it's set ridiculously high.<P>3rd- If you want Maybe a little fuel enrichment at WOT, but not even really necessary.<P>4th- Maybe a little timing advance at WOT like 2 degrees, again not necessary.<P>5th- Optional EGR shutdown.  No egr system operation. Since EGR is shut down at WOT anyway, it's only might help half throttle response only, but not significantly.<P>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT with nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||06-23-2000||04:08 PM||||Nope, no limiters on the 88. It will work in the 86-87's.<P>hyptnotisE: Are you talking about the decel cutoff when you say "depressurize"? <P>The V6 is set to 12:1 for AFR at WOT. It don't need more fuel, it needs less.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||HYPTNOTiSE||06-24-2000||07:49 AM||||yeah i'm talking about the decell cutoff, but i figured everyone would understand depressurize better.  i've never seen a fiero on an A/F that was actually 12:1 at WOT.  Shaun hammit's car is around 14:1, well he's never in the green under WOT.  so a little fuel enrichment would be nice there, especially with the nitrous, although i dont think the stock injectors are capable of flowing a 12:1 condition under nitrous.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||06-24-2000||10:13 AM||||Using a wideband O2 or the stock O2 sensor? 14:1 is dang lean. If it's the LED style that uses the stock O2, they're right only at 14.7:1. <P>Yeah, the stock injectors are small, but 16 lbs of fuel/hr * 6 is a lot of fuel.<P>Oh well, we beat this to death!<P>Terry<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||HYPTNOTiSE||06-24-2000||04:19 PM||||Yes no doubt that we would.<P>I'm going to be using 30lb injectors in my 3.2 rebuild.  I also got a piggyback fuel management computer, which alows me to run pretty much any injector i want.  It's pretty darn cool. Now that i have fuel management out of the way, i can work on a custom intake manfold setup for use of the Gen3 heads and the distributer.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bruce||06-24-2000||07:32 PM||||Save your money- the stock chip is fine.||||reg||1
